      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m wondering if the cleaner way to do this would be to check the busy bit during init, send a failure result if it\u0027s set, and then clear the bit. That way, this driver doesn\u0027t need to synchronize any internal state or worry about interrupts any more than it already does. Also, an after-the-sysjump change would only need to be an RW change, whereas a before-the-sysjump change would need to be an RO change. Would the AP generally be OK getting a late or out of context error response?\n\nRegarding the existing driver clearing it at init, maybe the negative response is also required to re-synchronize the AP? Just guessing.",
      "parentUuid": "475fcfde_8692ee7b",
      "revId": "0637942d4190ee31ee46aef36852e4e7a242f69e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
